"command":"py tools/bgrun.py --material --max-min 3 --log tools/bench/diag_c99c_prerun3.log -- py -u tools/stage_prerun.py --prerun tools/bench/diag_c99c_bench.py","timeout":30000,"description":"Offline pre-run of the revised bench script"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01TR6Pksmpa5NcJhH6DLcLTW","tool_input":{"command":"tasklist | grep -i labview; echo \"rc=$?\"","timeout":30000,"description":"Confirm no LabVIEW process remains"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01HzHJYDfDCj45UGrLRHYW83","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && py tools/bgrun.py --max-min 10 --log tools/bench/retro.log -- py tools/retrospective.py --cycle 99; tail -5 tools/bench/retro.log","timeout":660000,"description":"Run the cycle-99 retrospective under bgrun"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01LWBYMTM8H2oPRy2Jfsb1A5","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && sed -n '3152,$p' tools/bench/retro.log | grep -nE \"^VIOLATION|VERDICT|peer.ps1|BGRUN|ERROR|TIMEOUT|QUOTA|verdict_\" | cut -c1-500; ls tools/bench/cards/ | grep -i \"cycle99\"","timeout":30000,"description":"Show result lines of the cycle-99 retrospective run"}},{"tool_name":"Bash","tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZta15xuVbL5LKdBNkHGzx","tool_input":{"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\" && until [ \"$(grep -cE 'BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)' tools/bench/retro.log)\" -gt \"$(grep -c 'BGRUN START' tools/bench/retro.log | awk '{print $1-1}')\" ]; do sleep 5; done; tail -c 600 tools/bench/retro.log","description":"Wait for the cycle-99 retrospective END line","run_in_background":true}},{"tool_name":"Monitor","tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBzQBririsobwf7kA7JwCN","tool_input":{"description":"cycle-99 retrospective END line","timeout_ms":600000,"command":"cd \"G:/Codes/LabVIEW_Codes/MinLab/zz_LabView VI/AAA_UNIST/2. Tracking/V6_ParallelLoop\"; until tail -n 3 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -qE \"BGRUN (END|TIMEOUT|KILLED)\" && ! tail -n 3 tools/bench/retro.log | grep -q \"after 356s\"; do sleep 5; done; tail -n 3 tools/bench/retro.log | cut -c1-300"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":3,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":3,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":1,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":3,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{"material":2,"material-opus-max":1}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":59,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"Cycle 99 is closed: the separate display-loop design is written and judged GO, but no VI has been built yet.\n\n**What the measurements showed**\n- **The indicator is not the cost; the computation behind it is.** The ~10 ms per frame at 15 picks is For #1359's Median + FIR work feeding the Force-vs-Extension plot (#8323). Moving only #8323 would leave that 10 ms in the frame loop. So the design moves the plot's computation too: the node set Pre-decided 206(b) already identified. The ring insert and `Magnet2Force` stay in the frame loop because they feed the ring history.\n- **The Z/dZ items (#6085/#5696) are not display.** They feed the ring, so they are out of scope.\n- **The moved set costs at least 7.94 ms per frame at 15 beads.** This was measured on a scratch copy and is a lower bound.\n- **The cost of writing the 4.8 MB ring to a local each frame was not measured.** The scratch test VI broke (ExecState 0) four times while being built. The GO rests on an assumption, named in PD212(i)2: that write costs a few whole-array copies, about 1–3 ms in total. The acceptance run (15 picks, 120 s, alternating against `D1_s1_copy.vi`) measures the net gain directly. If the gain comes out under 5 ms, that write cost is the first thing to read.\n\n**Design (PD212, in `docs/d1-loop12-17-split-plan.md`)**\n- A new loop runs on its own clock (a `Display period (ms)` control, default 100 ms).\n- It reads the ring and the WLC element through locals.\n- It reads `Exp Baseline` and both half-width controls through locals. No control terminal moves, because moving a panel terminal into a loop body is what broke the scratch test VI.\n- It stops the same way loop #25380 already does, by reading `TurnOff`.\n- The one flag for you: at display time the two locals can come from adjacent frames. This affects only what is drawn, by at most one frame; saved data is untouched.\n\n**Next cycle (100):** write the stage rows offline, then build the missing scripting tools the rows need: `Wait (ms)`, `Visible = False`, and a way to write #8323. After that come the dry and pre-run checks, one LabVIEW run, and the acceptance run.\n\n**Retrospective:** it found one fault (`repeated-failure-class`, 25 min), and I accepted it. My cards 99-2/99-3 had GUI access turned off, which blocked the error-list reader, so the broken test VI was rebuilt without reading why. The rule is now in STATUS: a card that builds a VI can read the error list, and reads it before any second attempt.\n\n**Housekeeping:** `D1_s1_copy.vi` is unchanged, nothing was saved, and LabVIEW was closed after each card. `tools/bench/next.json` is valid. No new user decisions were added.\n\nThe Figma connector needs authorising in your claude.ai connector settings before it can be used.","ttft_ms":1852,"type":"result","duration_ms":5582068,"uuid":"97f663a5-8e5e-4ac5-b33e-d4c50c54f5f9","ttft_stream_ms":1791,"time_to_request_ms":224,"first_content_frame_ms":1791,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
